    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "New Orleans sits in a tight bend of the Mississippi River, upriver from the Gulf of Mexico, with Lake Pontchartrain to the north. The bend gave it the name Crescent City. Much of the city lies below sea level behind levees.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Jean-Baptiste Le Moyne de Bienville founded the city for France in 1718. Spain ruled it for nearly 40 years before the 1803 Louisiana Purchase, and most French Quarter buildings date from after the fires of 1788 and 1794. Jazz grew here in the early 1900s out of brass bands, blues and church music.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "February to May brings mild weather and the biggest festivals, Mardi Gras and Jazz Fest. Summer is hot and humid, and hurricane season runs from June to November.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
